      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If your roof insurance claim is denied, read the denial letter line by line to identify the exact reason (such as wear-and-tear, age, or missed deadlines), then get an independent inspection and file a formal appeal.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "get an independent inspection and file a formal appeal"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Steps to Take After a Denial"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Read the Denial Letter: Check the specific policy clauses, exclusions, or reasons cited by the insurer (e.g., normal wear and tear versus acute storm or wind damage).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get an Independent Inspection: Hire a reputable, licensed roofing contractor to perform a thorough, documented inspection. Have them take detailed photo grids, look for hail spatter or wind uplift, and write a professional report.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Request a Re-Inspection: Ask your insurance company for a re-inspection and have your independent roofer present on the roof with the adjuster.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              1,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "File a Formal Appeal: Package your contractor's report, local weather data for the date of loss, and a written rebuttal quoting your policy language back to the insurer. Send it via certified mail.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              2,
              4
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Escalate if Needed: If the insurer still refuses to pay a valid claim, consider hiring a public adjuster , filing a complaint with your state's department of insurance, or consulting an insurance attorney.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "public adjuster",
                "link": "https://www.experian.com/blogs/ask-experian/what-to-do-if-homeowners-insurance-claim-is-denied/"
              }
            ],
            "reference_indexes": [
              4,
              5
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like to share why the insurance company said they denied it or what kind of damage your roof has (wind, hail, leaks), I can help you figure out the best way to respond."
      }
    ],
